#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0460 expect=violation domain=AE
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when the High Level Term (--HLT) is not on the MedDRA primary system organ class hierarchy path.
#note "Q6b construction pin (PLAN-dictionary-seeder Phase 5 debt, closed in Phase 7b): the dummy meddra hierarchy is what MedDraConverter builds from primary_soc_fg='Y' mdhier rows ONLY. The HLT 'Central nervous system haemorrhages and cerebrovascular accidents' is multiaxial in the notional mdhier behind the dummy: its Y-row reaches SOC 'Nervous system disorders' (in the hierarchy), while an N-row reaches SOC 'Vascular disorders' through the same HLGT (deliberately NOT in the hierarchy, though 'Vascular disorders' IS a levels.SOC term). Row 1 pairs the HLT with that secondarily-reachable SOC and must FIRE - --SOC is defined to carry the PRIMARY SOC, so a secondary axis is off-path. Under a full-closure construction the same row would be on-path and quiet, which is exactly what the older fixtures (whose wrong SOC is unreachable under EITHER construction) could not discriminate. Row 2 uses the primary SOC and stays quiet. If a converter change to full closure is ever ported into the dummy, this scenario goes red - that is its job."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#dictionaries dummy
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col AEHLT type=Char label="High Level Term"
col AESOC type=Char label="Primary System Organ Class"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 1 | Central nervous system haemorrhages and cerebrovascular accidents | Vascular disorders
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 2 | Central nervous system haemorrhages and cerebrovascular accidents | Nervous system disorders
---
